          "basis": "X",
          "sleep": 1.0,
          "options": "on",
          "shots": 1000
        }
      ]
    },
    "T4": {
      "question": "Is idling inside a circuit (transport layers) the same noise as sleep?",
      "decision": "4 qubits in |+>, L layers of [barrier; RZZ(0) on a random pairing], as in Quantinuum's memory benchmark. Idle part = rate(on) - rate(off) at L = 64; with the T3 curve it converts to seconds per layer. Also: does the rate grow with L at all (L = 0, 16, 64)?",
      "runs": [
        {
          "name": "T4_transport_L0_on",
          "kind": "transport",
          "n": 4,
          "layers": 0,
          "options": "on",
          "shots": 1000
        },
        {
          "name": "T4_transport_L16_on",
          "kind": "transport",
          "n": 4,
          "layers": 16,
          "options": "on",
          "shots": 1000
        },
        {
          "name": "T4_transport_L64_on",
          "kind": "transport",
          "n": 4,
          "layers": 64,
          "options": "on",
          "shots": 1000
        },
        {
          "name": "T4_transport_L64_off",
          "kind": "transport",
          "n": 4,
          "layers": 64,
          "options": "off",
          "shots": 1000
        }
      ]
    },
    "T5a": {
      "question": "Do sleeps on different qubits run at the same time or one after another?",
      "decision": "4 qubits in |+>, sleep(0.25) on each in turn. Error ~ P(0.25 s) (~0.5%) -> concurrent; ~ P(1 s) (~7-9%) -> serial.",
      "runs": [
        {
          "name": "T5a_sleep_each_0p25",
          "kind": "concurrency",
          "n": 4,
          "sleep": 0.25,
          "options": "on",
          "shots": 1000
        }
      ]
    },
    "T5": {
      "question": "How long does a d = 3 syndrome round take?",
      "decision": "8 targets in |+> wait (barriers) while the d = 3 X-memory circuit runs 5 rounds (one reused ancilla). Idle part = rate(on) - rate(off); inverting the T3 curve gives the block's idle time, / rounds = round time. A difference consistent with 0 gives an upper bound.",
      "runs": [
        {
          "name": "T5_rounds5_on",
          "kind": "rounds",
          "targets": 8,
          "rounds": 5,
          "options": "on",
          "shots": 1000
        },
        {
          "name": "T5_rounds5_off",
          "kind": "rounds",
          "targets": 8,
          "rounds": 5,
          "options": "off",
          "shots": 1000
        }
      ]
    }
  },
